 "notes": [
  "Each arm ran twice in fresh processes, interleaved; tables report the mean of the two runs. Per-category decode is the median of five scored requests; prefill is the median of eight scored requests per depth.",
  "Weighted decode uses the BetterBench category weights listed in profile.weighted_decode_weights; chat and math are reported but carry no weight.",
  "All arms ran with GPU_MAX_HW_QUEUES=1 and the same allocator setting, so every process was in the same decode timing mode (C1 decode forward-time median recorded per run). The gains therefore exclude the effect of the queue setting, which the 26 September image sets by default.",
  "The BetterBench W3A4 runs used an earlier calibration of the same 3-bit format; tensor layout and runtime are identical, so the timing applies to the published weights. Accuracy and the four-request run at the launcher's default KV budget used the published weights.",
  "The W3A4 arm ran the release image itself (local image ID identical to the release tag); its registry digest is added when the image is published.",
  "W3A4 changes greedy outputs (5 of 12 greedy prompts identical to MXFP4) because its weights are lossy; each W3A4 run reproduced its own 12 greedy outputs after the benchmark and across both processes. The MXFP4 arm of this round matched all 12 greedy outputs of the 24 September release.",
  "Sampled output content and accepted-token work can differ; these are serving-throughput measurements, not identical-output timing.",
  "Nominal prefill depths correspond to median actual prompt lengths 1516.5, 5894.5, 11802, 23549.5, 47016.5."
